                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Midland/Odessa TX",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 25 at 1:49PM MDT until September 26 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Midland/Odessa TX",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southeast New Mexico, including the following\nareas, Central Lea, Eddy County Plains, Guadalupe Mountains of Eddy\nCounty and Northern Lea and southwest Texas, including the\nfollowing areas, Chinati Mountains, Davis Mountains, Davis\nMountains Foothills, Eastern Culberson, Guadalupe Mountains Above\n7000 Feet, Guadalupe and Delaware Mountains, Marfa Plateau,\nPresidio Valley and Van Horn and Highway 54 Corridor.\n\n* WHEN...Through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional rounds of showers and thunderstorms will continue to\ndevelop over the Watch area today through this evening. Heavy\nrainfall may quickly result in areas of flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
